<title>INDIA: India's HPCL 1996/97 net higher.</title>
<headline>India's HPCL 1996/97 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		   6,122.2     vs     5,142.4</p>
<p>    Sales turnover	   180,890.0    vs    148,620.0</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)		 29.31    vs	  25.33</p>
<p>    Div (in rupeees)		 4.0     vs	   3.5</p>
<p>    Income		     139,414.5     vs   118,662.8</p>
<p>    Other income		 1,701.5     vs     1,027.4</p>
<p>    Total expenditure	127,794.5     vs   108,784.0</p>
<p>    Interest			 975.2     vs	 462.1</p>
<p>    Gross profit		12,346.3     vs    10,444.1</p>
<p>    Depreciation		 2,929.3     vs	1,984.6</p>
<p>    Tax			    3,294.8     vs	3,317.1</p>
<p>Note: State-run Hindustan Petroleum Corporation Ltd (HPCL) said total sales volume was at an all-time high at 15.46 million tonnes, up 9.3 percent over the previous year, compared to an industry growth of 6.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Bombay equities desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
